From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Heinemeier Hansson <david@hey.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:52:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PM / devfreq: qcom-scmi-memlat: disable polling by default

CPUCP runs DDR/LLCC DVFS autonomously once MEMLAT_START_TIMER is started.
Setting profile->polling_ms to cpucp_sample_ms / 2 (2 ms on every SoC
this driver supports: Glymur, X1E80100, and X1P42100, all of which use
cpucp_sample_ms = 4) polls all three devfreq devices (ddr, ddr-qos,
llcc) at 500 Hz each solely to populate sysfs trans_stat. On an idle
ASUS Zenbook A16 (UX3607OA), that generates ~1,625 IRQs/s on
apss_cpucp_mbox, ~865 wakeups/s on devfreq_wq, and holds CPU0 in WFI
37.4% of the time.

Leave profile->polling_ms at 0 so the remote governor does not arm a
periodic monitor timer. Hardware DVFS scaling (verified up to 4761 MHz
DDR / 1211 MHz LLCC) and on-demand cur_freq reads continue working.
Note that trans_stat stays frozen at initial_freq with zero recorded
transitions while polling is off; userspace can still opt in to
trans_stat sampling by writing a non-zero polling_interval.

Measured on ASUS Zenbook A16 UX3607OA (7.3.6-5-omarchy with
polling_interval=0 across ddr, ddr-qos, and llcc): apss_cpucp_mbox
drops from ~1,625/s to 0-7/s (-99.6%), devfreq_wq from 865/s to 0/s,
and CPU0 WFI from 37.4% to 2.3%.
---
 drivers/devfreq/scmi-qcom-memlat-devfreq.c | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/devfreq/scmi-qcom-memlat-devfreq.c b/drivers/devfreq/scmi-qcom-memlat-devfreq.c
index 9ca85b2..017cde3 100644
--- a/drivers/devfreq/scmi-qcom-memlat-devfreq.c
+++ b/drivers/devfreq/scmi-qcom-memlat-devfreq.c
@@ -1176,12 +1176,15 @@ static int scmi_qcom_memlat_configure_events(struct scmi_device *sdev,
 		struct devfreq_dev_profile *profile = &memory->profile;
 
 		/*
-		 * CPUCP re-evaluates and re-votes at most once per cpucp_sample_ms,
-		 * so a new operating point can appear only that often. Polling at half
-		 * that period guarantees each distinct vote is observed in trans_stat
-		 * before it can change again.
+		 * CPUCP runs hardware DVFS autonomously once MEMLAT_START_TIMER is
+		 * enabled. Polling the SCMI mailbox at cpucp_sample_ms / 2 across
+		 * every memlat device only populates sysfs trans_stat while causing
+		 * a continuous idle interrupt and workqueue storm. Leave polling
+		 * off by default: cur_freq remains live on demand, while trans_stat
+		 * stays frozen at initial_freq until userspace opts in by writing a
+		 * non-zero polling_interval.
 		 */
-		profile->polling_ms = max(1U, info->cfg_data->cpucp_sample_ms / 2);
+		profile->polling_ms = 0;
 		profile->get_cur_freq = scmi_qcom_devfreq_get_cur_freq;
 		profile->initial_freq = range->max_freq_khz > 1 ?
 					(unsigned long)((u64)range->min_freq_khz * HZ_PER_KHZ) :
-- 
